.Plugin IDs
    Tenable Plugin  : 21156 (Windows Compliance Checks)
    Audit File      : DISA Microsoft Windows 10 STIG v3r4
    STIG ID         : WN10-AU-000500
    Vuln ID         : V-220779
    CCI             : CCI-001849

.TESTED ON
    Date(s) Tested  : 2025-09-11
    Tested By       : Juan Saravia
    Systems Tested  : Windows 10 Pro (22H2), Windows 11 Pro (23H2)
    PowerShell Ver. : 5.1, 7.4

.USAGE
    Run this script in an elevated PowerShell session (Run as Administrator). 
    It will create or correct the "MaxSize" value under the Application Event Log registry key.
    If the value already exists with the correct size, no changes are made.

    Example syntax:
        PS C:\> .\Set-EventLogMaxSize.ps1

    Optional usage:
        - Save the script in a centralized repository for compliance or remediation tasks.
        - Deploy via Intune, SCCM, or Group Policy as part of your hardening baseline.
#>

# Enforces Windows Application Event Log MaxSize registry setting (STIG WN10-AU-000500)

$regPath   = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\EventLog\Application"
$valueName = "MaxSize"
$valueData = 0x00032768  # Decimal: 208,896 (32 MB)

# Ensure the registry path exists
if (-not (Test-Path $regPath)) {
    New-Item -Path $regPath -Force | Out-Null
}

# Check, create, or correct the value
$currentValue = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -Name $valueName -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).$valueName
if ($null -eq $currentValue) {
    New-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -Name $valueName -Value $valueData -PropertyType DWord -Force | Out-Null
    Write-Output "Registry value created: $regPath\$valueName = $valueData"
}
elseif ($currentValue -ne $valueData) {
    Set-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -Name $valueName -Value $valueData
    Write-Output "Registry value updated: $regPath\$valueName corrected to $valueData"
}
else {
    Write-Output "Registry value already set correctly."
}
